## I found a ridiculous UK dataset we should ingest immediately

HMRC's **UK Trade Info API is completely open and doesn't even require authentication**.

It exposes commodities, monthly imports, exports, countries, ports **and individual traders**. 

For HS `847950` — industrial robots — the public trader search currently finds **497 businesses trading the category during 2026**, including ABB Robotics UK, Applied Automation and individual manufacturers/end users. ([UK Trade Info][3])

This means we can reconstruct:

```text
who imports robots
what months they import
their postcode
commodity
source country
value
mass / supplementary quantity where available
```

Then:

```text
HMRC trader
    ↓
Companies House
    ↓
facility/location
    ↓
sector
    ↓
company accounts
    ↓
jobs
    ↓
procurement
    ↓
robot deployment evidence
```

That is far better than merely estimating UK adoption from IFR.

And HMRC has **bulk imports/exports and trader files going back to 2016**, plus current monthly replacements and an API. 

I'd make this one of POWRobots' crown-jewel datasets.

