# Historical data is actually excellent

| Data                       | History / resolution                                                          | Why it matters                                                                                                      |
| -------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **IFR World Robotics**     | Installations + operational stock **1993–2025**, country/application/industry | Ground-truth robot adoption baseline; premium data currently €2,500 ([IFR International Federation of Robotics][4]) |
| **HMRC UK Trade Info**     | Detailed monthly UK data; trader files since 2016                             | Actual UK robot/component importers and exporters                                                                   |
| **UN Comtrade**            | Long global trade history                                                     | China→UK and supplier-country flows; official Python package exists ([GitHub][5])                                   |
| **China NBS**              | Monthly industrial/service robot production                                   | Direct upstream cycle signal; official government data ([National Bureau of Statistics][6])                         |
| **MIR Databank**           | Quarterly China robotics/automation data                                      | Supplier, product and downstream-industry sales data ([MIR Industry][7])                                            |
| **Company filings**        | Years of A-share/HK filings                                                   | shipments, capacity, revenue, product mix, margins, capex                                                           |
| **ROS/GitHub**             | Git history + robot descriptions                                              | machine-readable robot family/model ontology                                                                        |
| **Component distributors** | Start snapshots now                                                           | price/inventory/lead-time history that becomes proprietary                                                          |
| **Used markets**           | Start snapshots now                                                           | installed-base/repair/depreciation signals                                                                          |

IFR is probably worth buying eventually because their query database gives us 30+ years of installations and operational stock. But we don't need it to begin.

