# RBTX is especially interesting

This might be the single coolest existing source I found for POWRobots.

**RBTX by igus** is basically an online robotics-component marketplace.

It includes:

```text
robots
end effectors
vision
control systems
pneumatics
software
services
accessories
```

and its UK site exposes actual GBP pricing. For example, it currently lists robot cells, axes, profiles and complete solutions with explicit prices. ([RBTX][20])

There are **350+ products from 80+ partners** on the UK offering, while the broader platform claims hundreds of application templates. ([igus UK][21])

Even better, they operate China pricing too. Their Chinese marketplace currently shows things such as Fairino, DOBOT and igus robot arms priced directly in yuan. ([RBTX][22])

So we can potentially construct:

```text
DOBOT / Fairino / igus model
China price
EU price
UK price
payload
reach
configuration
accessory stack
integration price
```

and preserve changes.

**That is almost exactly the experiment we want.**

