# Who are we competing with?

The market is fragmented, which is good.

| Existing player       | Their strength                                                    | Missing from their product                           |
| --------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |
| **IFR**               | Canonical global adoption statistics                              | Product/parts pricing, stocks, real-time bottlenecks |
| **MIR Databank**      | Excellent China industrial-market intelligence                    | UK downstream/repair/parts graph                     |
| **Interact Analysis** | Serious industrial robotics and components research               | Open longitudinal part-level market state            |
| **HowToRobot**        | 20,000+ global robotics/automation suppliers ([How to Robot][23]) | Physical bottleneck/investment history               |
| **RBTX**              | Priced robots/components + compatibility                          | Macro supply-chain/equity intelligence               |
| **Octopart/Nexar**    | Electronics supply-chain data                                     | Robot-specific BOM/use/repair mapping                |
| **Findchips**         | Electronics prices/inventory                                      | Robotics context                                     |
| **GGII**              | Deep China robotics research                                      | UK physical-market graph                             |
| **MIR**               | China manufacturer/industry quarterly sales                       | granular daily parts/landed spreads                  |

Interact Analysis is particularly validating. Their industrial-robot-components work explicitly tracks **motors, drives, precision gearboxes, controllers, teach pendants, sensors, end effectors and machine vision**, and estimated this component market above $10.5bn as far back as 2021. ([Interact Analysis][24])

So we're not imagining that components matter.

The opening is:

> **Nobody appears to own the public-facing longitudinal graph connecting specific robot architectures and component families to China production/pricing, international trade, UK prices/inventory, UK adoption, repair capacity and listed-company exposure.**

That's the product.

